{"type":"record","name":"IbkrPreOpenOwnership","namespace":"app.options.ibkr.gex","doc":"Which mode owns the trade date, under the reserved key __ownership|<tradeDate>. Published to options.ibkr.gex.status.v2 by databento-gex-service's pre-open IBKR GEX publisher (IbkrPreOpenService). The predecessor topic options.ibkr.gex.status carried hand-built JSON strings until 2026-10-17; this record reproduces that JSON FIELD FOR FIELD AND NAME FOR NAME. That is a hard requirement, not tidiness: the feed gateway converts these records to JSON for the browser with AvroJson, which emits exactly the published record's own fields, and option-chain.js reads them BY NAME. Renaming or retyping a field here changes what the browser receives. The registry subject is this record's FULL NAME, under RecordNameStrategy. That is deliberate and not the Confluent default, and here it is load-bearing rather than merely conventional: this ONE topic carries nine distinct value shapes, and a topic-name subject could not hold nine schemas. It also keeps one subject across environments, where TopicNameStrategy would mint a different subject per environment because the topic name carries the environment's TOPIC_PREFIX.","fields":[{"name":"ownerMode","type":"string","doc":"The owning mode for this trade date."},{"name":"outputGeneration","type":"long","doc":"The generation minted when ownership was taken."},{"name":"effectiveTimeMs","type":"long","doc":"When ownership became effective, in epoch milliseconds. The browser anchors its server clock from the first present of serverTimeMs, eventTimeMs, atMs, effectiveTimeMs, so this field's NAME is part of the contract."}]}